// Typechecks the ACL test surface, which `tsconfig.json` excludes from the
// build (tests must not emit into dist/).
//
// Without this, tests are transpile-only under vitest: a test can call a method
// that no longer exists and stay green until it happens to run that line. That
// is not hypothetical — the v2 ACL port left every test file calling the deleted
// `permittedActions`/`Scope` API while `tsc` reported zero errors.
//
// SCOPE: deliberately narrow. The wider suite carries ~176 pre-existing type
// errors from never having been checked (unrelated to authorization — agent
// step config shapes, builder generics, service registry). Adopting those is its
// own task; this config is a ratchet over the area we are actively rewriting, so
// it must stay at zero. Widen it file-by-file as that debt gets paid down.
//
// `src/connectors/core/**` is in scope because those tests are new — no
// inherited debt — and because one asserts a COMPILE-TIME guarantee with
// `@ts-expect-error`. A directive in a file nobody typechecks proves nothing.
// Deliberately not `src/connectors/**`: the built-in step tests moved in from
// `steps/builtin/` carrying the same unchecked-test debt as the rest of the
// suite, and adopting it is its own task.
//
// `src/testing/**` is in scope on purpose: the conformance kit ships as test
// code for hosts to run against their own adapters, so it must not drift from
// the port silently — the exact failure mode this ACL work exists to remove.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "src/authz/**/*.ts",
    "src/testing/**/*.ts",
    "src/runtime/authz-coverage.test.ts",
    "src/runtime/authz-enforcement.test.ts",
    "src/runtime/folder-acl.test.ts",
    "src/runtime/attributes.test.ts",
    "src/router/authz-router.test.ts",
    "src/persistence/in-memory-adapter.test.ts",
    "src/connectors/core/**/*.test.ts",
    // The trigger surface: its generics exist to make a wrong payload or config a
    // COMPILE error, and a `@ts-expect-error` in a file nobody typechecks proves
    // nothing. In scope because these tests are new — no inherited debt.
    "src/triggers/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/ingest/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/util/**/*.test.ts",
    // The attachment surface: `Attachment` carries a handle rather than bytes,
    // and the adapter is stream-only. Both are new or wholly rewritten, so
    // there is no inherited debt — and a test that still builds the old shape
    // is exactly the drift this file exists to stop. It already happened once:
    // nine workflow-ui tests kept constructing `{ data }` after the rename and
    // stayed green, because that package typechecked no tests at all. It
    // does now — see `workflow-ui/tsconfig.test.json`.
    "src/storage/**/*.ts",
    "src/completion/**/*.ts",
    "src/common/multipart-values.test.ts",
    "src/connectors/builtin/steps/multipart-body.test.ts",
    "src/engine/gate-addressing-in-loops.test.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
